In a similar vein as my previous experiments, I've turned up another bug
relating to water and lava, this time involving water walking boots: 

If one takes off a pair of said boots while standing on water, one
obviously falls into the water.  However if the boots are removed while
standing on lava they don't fall into the lava; therefore one can also
take exactly one step onto lava with non-fireproof water walking boots
(destroying them) and not become stuck in the lava.  This is a clear
inconsistency which I view as a bug.

This is fairly easy to reproduce, so go ahead and try it.


